    "/mygrain-wavs::Guy-sitting-next-to-me-on-the-bus-has-been-listening-to-the-same-goddamn-drum-beat-for-an-hour-already-.120-1.wav": {
      "comment": "Like what I\u2019ve done here? \nI THOUGHT of this already. Stop taking my ideas.\nDid you? I knew that.\nYou know it's just more ways for us to be obnoxious to eachother. I guess I'll accept.....\nI like everything you\u2019ve done so far, but I\u2019m not going to go through them all and like them - I\u2019m not a stalker.\nI like what you've done too, I saved some of your stuff maybe to use later? I don't mind if you stalk me. Just you though.\nThis stuff is gold, really. It\u2019s what I\u2019ve been wanting for a long time. There are so many song \u2018starters\u2019 here. It\u2019s probably for a different genre than I move in, but I can see it inspiring me. I\u2019m very pleased with this. I love stuff like this. It was kind of what I was looking for with infiltrator and shade. It needs a proper export so you can recall stuff and maybe transpose it or make variations. That makes it more flexible for songs. It\u2019s probably cost about $500 dollars in API credits so far \ud83d\ude2c Oh well. Money is just a concept\u2026\nI suspect the rendering is a little dodgy at the moment. I think there is a little space or blip at the start so they will need to be trimmed in the daw. Will sort that.\nFixed the rendering I hope.\nIt's my dream to sit and make sounds all day. Not only that but the random features makes it feel like a slot machine. Dangerously lovely. \u2764\ufe0f I'm captured.",
      "fileName": "Guy-sitting-next-to-me-on-the-bus-has-been-listening-to-the-same-goddamn-drum-beat-for-an-hour-already-.120-1.wav",
      "reaction": "love",
      "routeBase": "/mygrain-wavs",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-08T09:21:18Z"
